    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and verified. Here's what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n## Root Cause\nCommander.js was not properly capturing the `--ci` flag when using variadic `[args...]` with `allowUnknownOption(true)`. The flag was being swallowed by the parser and not passed through to the frai-gate subprocess.\n\n## The Fix\nChanged the `gate` command handler in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to bypass Commander.js's argument parser and directly access `process.argv`. This ensures all arguments after 'gate' (including flags like `--ci`) are passed through to the frai-gate CLI:\n\n```typescript\n// Before: Used Commander.js parsed args (which lost the --ci flag)\n.action(async (args: string[]) => {\n  // ...\n  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...(args ?? [])], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n})\n\n// After: Uses process.argv directly to capture all arguments\n.action(async () => {\n  const gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\n  const gateArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : [];\n  // ...\n  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...gateArgs], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n})\n```\n\n## Verification\n\u2705 Rebuilt the frai-cli package with `pnpm --filter frai build`  \n\u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` and confirmed both files are created:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` \u2713\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713\n\nThe workflow file has the correct GitHub Actions configuration.",
